WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.930
- Songwriting is about your experiences,

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.070
and it expands your vocabulary

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.960
in terms of the way you see the world.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.930
Music is something that
people can connect with

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:11.730
and feel an emotion.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.280
There was a few really
cool underground spots

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.750
where I would go and
listen to jazz in Dubai

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.190
and I'd see all these musicians

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.590
and I'd be like yeah
that's where I wanna be at.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.060
- I'm Anna Devis.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.670
- I am Daniel Rueda.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.430
- Together, we are
architects and photographers.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.620
- [Daniel] Our approach is
to play with perspectives

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.370
and geometry within an urban landscape.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.360
- [Anna] And as architects,
we travel the world

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.720
exploring and seeing aspects of buildings

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.490
so we can tell stories through the image.

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.080
- [Daniel] We are on a
journey to meet with other

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:43.450
like-minded and inspiring

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:44.663
creatives in Dubai.

00:00:49.066 --> 00:00:50.420
- [Anna] Here, we meet with Layla Kardan,

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.290
a bold new performer who is
breaking perceptions of what

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.830
it means to be a female
singer in the Middle East.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.520
- [Daniel] We first meet Layla in Dubai's

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.201
old neighborhood of Al Fahidi.

00:00:59.201 --> 00:01:00.660
(traditional oud music)

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.460
- I think, both of you being architects,

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.440
you can appreciate that
it's such a completely

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.258
different architecture to what
you typically see in Dubai.

00:01:08.258 --> 00:01:09.091
- Yeah.

00:01:09.091 --> 00:01:11.360
- [Daniel] Yeah, not many
skyscrapers around here.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:13.610
- We were living in
Australia and my father

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.240
was really excited about
the great opportunity

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.580
in Dubai, so he moved us here.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:21.110
It was such a different
world to what I'd seen,

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:22.972
you know, growing up in
Sydney, but it became,

00:01:22.972 --> 00:01:24.790
you know, a home for us.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:27.220
I have really beautiful
memories as a child

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.670
growing up in Dubai and got to learn a lot

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.140
about the culture.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.400
You really feel the
history and the heritage

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.550
of the people when you come to the creek.

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:39.460
Really interesting
alleyways in these bazaars

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.380
where you'll see spice
markets, fabric merchants,

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:44.210
sellers of antique jewelry,

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:47.840
and all of that is a feast for the eyes.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.750
I like to reference traditional
Middle Eastern instruments,

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:53.850
just because I love the sounds of them.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:57.630
But in a subtle way, I like
the oud more as a drum beat,

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.853
and warp it and distort
it, but it's still there.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:04.680
- It's a very clever way to make a very

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.150
historical instrument not
too lost in the history

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.840
and use it in a more contemporary way.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.190
I think it's fascinating, actually.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.190
(slow piano chords)

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.480
- [Anna] Even though you feel
you are in such a modern city,

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.700
you know you are in Dubai,
you are not in America

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.720
or in Europe because they always have this

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.720
traditional touch in everything they do.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.350
- [Daniel] At night, the
whole city comes to life

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:34.840
and we begin to understand
how Dubai's music scene

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:37.313
has become a crucial part
of the nightlife here.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.090
- [Layla] In the last three years,

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.290
there's live music all over town.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:45.080
Before we would go to this
one spot to watch Jazz music,

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:48.089
and now you can, in one
night, I can name like seven

00:02:48.089 --> 00:02:50.283
or eight or even more places.

00:02:53.483 --> 00:02:56.650
♪ Yeah yeah yeah yeah ♪

00:02:57.519 --> 00:02:58.713
- [Anna] Wanting to share a more intimate

00:02:58.713 --> 00:03:00.730
side to the music scene,

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:02.660
Layla invites us to an after party,

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.530
where we meet the community of musicians

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.080
that she collaborates with.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.530
- Guys, this is a complete jam,

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.900
so we don't even know
what we're doing, sorry.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.570
And that's another thing
I love about Dubai,

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:14.970
is that I've got an
incredible band of musicians

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.136
from all over the world.

00:03:17.136 --> 00:03:19.220
(upbeat jazz music)

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.710
Wherever you go in the world,

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:25.710
it's important to see the
culture and the music.

00:03:25.818 --> 00:03:27.748
♪ Guilded ♪

00:03:27.748 --> 00:03:30.580
♪ I wanted it golden ♪

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:33.470
I think it's the first thing
that teaches us tolerance is

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:36.330
when you understand a little
bit about a person's culture

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.340
and where they're from.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:41.862
Music is a very beautiful
way to share a message.

00:03:41.862 --> 00:03:43.880
♪ No place to go ♪

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:46.280
- [Anna] This day with Layla
has given us opportunity

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:48.700
to see Dubai's strong artistic circle.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.570
Allowing inspiration and
vision among musicians

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.388
to be shared through collaboration.

00:03:53.388 --> 00:03:54.221
♪ No place to go ♪

00:03:54.221 --> 00:03:56.750
- An experience we won't
forget in a music scene

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.713
we were unaware of before coming.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:01.655
Yes, sir!

00:04:01.655 --> 00:04:04.655
(light guitar solo)

